      "notes": "All claims are appropriately tiered. The stated claim correctly quotes M. Measurable claims (E13, E21) are drawn from plausible secondary sources and are consistent with the quotes. Projected claims (E16, E6) are not overstated \u2014 distributional framing uses 'would' language. The IEA (advocacy) source for E2 is correctly flagged in the rationale with a caution. The E13 source (freepricecompare.com) is media/commercial but is not the sole basis for the verdict \u2014 it is corroborated by E12/E14 and noted as a secondary figure. The fuel duty distributional claim (E6) uses a freeze rather than a 20p cut as the basis, which the claim correctly notes ('smaller than a 20p cut'). No tier blurring, no lever leakage, no party identity language, no motive attribution. The 'improves' direction is well-supported: all three components reduce household tax burden by construction; distributional caveats are noted but do not negate the directional finding. False balance is not an issue as direction is 'improves', not mixed. One minor observation: E13 is sourced from freepricecompare.com (commercial) and nesta.org.uk; the Nesta backing provides sufficient institutional grounding. Overall the verdict is internally consistent and evidence-led."
